error[LK0001]: `$` is not a character Link recognises
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.link:13:20
   |
13 |     let tagged = 1 $ 2
   |                    ^ unexpected character

error[LK0006]: malformed `\u` escape
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.link:14:19
   |
14 |     let path = "C:\users"
   |                   ^^ malformed escape
   |
   = note: a `\u` escape needs braces, as in `\u{1F600}`

error[LK0007]: unterminated string literal
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.link:15:16
   |
15 |     let open = "never closed
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this string has no closing `"`

error[LK0009]: `q` is not a valid numeric literal suffix
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.link:16:21
   |
16 |     let counted = 42q
   |                     ^ unknown suffix
   |
   = note: the suffixes are `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `f32` and `f64`

error[LK0010]: `2` is not a valid digit in a binary literal
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.link:17:21
   |
17 |     let mask = 0b1012
   |                     ^ invalid digit

error[LK0003]: tabs are not allowed in indentation
  --> tests/ui/several_errors_in_one_file.link:18:1
   |
18 | 	let indented_with_a_tab = 0
   | ^ tab character in the indentation
   |
   = note: Link does not interpret tabs: their width depends on how the file is displayed, so a block would mean different things to different readers. Indent with spaces only.
